WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.960
- [Kelly] I am so happy, you're hilarious.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:02.793
- [Abby] Oh, Thank you.

00:00:02.793 --> 00:00:04.620
- And, I mean, super talented actor.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.333
I always love comedians when they act,

00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:08.570
Y'all can go so dark or you like heavy

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.890
or you can go really light and funny,

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.342
It's awesome to watch you.

00:00:11.342 --> 00:00:14.200
- Yeah, I feel like
comedy, you have to be able

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.980
to really act and sell it.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:16.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:18.250
- Because, it's a lot.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.720
- Alright, well, do you have any plans

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.610
for Valentine's Day?

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.172
Are you one of those
people that goes all out?

00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:27.370
- We do, we definitely eat
a lot together, always.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.520
- [Kelly] That's like
a day that ends in Y.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.390
- Yeah, We'll just
binge and drink, we're..

00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:36.406
- [Justin] What are you drinking?

00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:37.689
- Just wine.

00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:38.750
- Okay, alright.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.590
- [Kelly] Red girl,
white girl? Just curious.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.423
- [Abby] Red.

00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:42.690
- Nice, me too, Pinot Noir.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.190
- Pinot Noir, yeah.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.270
- I heard something about you though,

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.100
that you've always wanted
to be a mom, right?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.468
- Yes, and we are doing
IVF right now actually.

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:52.301
(crowd cheers)

00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:53.134
Thank you.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.590
- It sounds like just a process

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.960
cause so many people go through it now,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.793
it sounds like a process,

00:00:58.793 --> 00:00:59.626
but it's kind of hardcore,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.110
I've had friends go through that.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.440
- Yeah, so this Valentine's day,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.746
I'll be getting shots in my butt.

00:01:05.746 --> 00:01:07.167
(laughs loudly)

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.000
- Hormones.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.833
- But my husband is very romantic.

00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:11.600
Yes hormones, but the
hormones are very intense

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.490
and you know, so many people,

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.077
they go through this.

00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:15.910
- [Kelly] So many.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.800
- And, you know, we don't
talk about it enough,

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.150
I think as women, and just,

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.270
we need to raise more understanding

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.103
and awareness behind it.

00:01:23.103 --> 00:01:24.210
- [Kelly] And I'm glad,
that's why I was so happy

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.270
you wanted to talk about this today,

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.980
because I have friends
that went through it,

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.440
and I mean, went through
some serious depression,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.940
felt shame, was like,
"What is wrong with me?",

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.870
like tried everything under the sun

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.950
and sometimes it just doesn't happen

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:36.970
and you just need science

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.230
to kind of help move it along.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.240
- Yeah and it's actually,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.600
it's such a miracle what they can do,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.300
like that's a miracle in of itself.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.133
- [Kelly] Agreed.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.860
Did you always picture
yourself being a mom?

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.350
- Yeah, definitely.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.590
- You're the baby of the family

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.900
and you always wanted kids?

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.150
We're like opposite humans.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.670
- No, I'm the older sister.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.697
- [Kelly] Oh, you're the
older, that makes sense.

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:57.010
- [Abby] But I had a little baby carriage

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.440
that I would, you know, and a baby doll.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.273
- [Kelly] Oh, that was my sister,

00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:00.110
and then she would curl my hair

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.356
and accidentally burn me, it was fine.

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:02.630
But you're...

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:04.237
- Yeah, I cut my sister's bangs a lot.

00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:06.530
- Yeah, that's what my sister would do.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.700
So your dad is comedian Chris Elliot,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.520
was that intimidating for your husband

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.710
to like meet the fam?

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.880
- [Abby] Oh, yeah for sure.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.050
- [Kelly] Cause he's hilarious.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.660
- [Abby] Yeah, there was a hazing period

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.034
for a while with Billy.

00:02:18.034 --> 00:02:19.402
- A hazing period? Oh, tell us.

00:02:19.402 --> 00:02:20.235
(laughs loudly)

00:02:20.235 --> 00:02:21.360
- Yeah, with my husband
coming into the family.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.490
We do this thing in our family

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.170
called the Ice Bucket Challenge,

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.460
but it's not the one for charity,

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.080
it's not the good one,
it's just to sober us up

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.074
when we've been drinking too much.

00:02:30.074 --> 00:02:32.870
(laughs loudly)

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.880
So what we do is, we all stick our head in

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:35.713
like a bucket of ice

00:02:35.713 --> 00:02:38.130
to see who can last the longest in there,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.780
and then whoever does, wins.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.127
- I would totally do this.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.960
- So my husband came to a wedding,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.810
actually it was the first time

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.720
I was introducing him to my parents and..

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.100
- [Kelly] The first time you introduced

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.830
your boyfriend to your
parents was at a wedding?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.770
- Yeah, my cousin's wedding.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.109
- [Kelly] That is bold.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.942
- Yeah.

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:57.775
- [Justin] I like it.

00:02:57.775 --> 00:03:00.200
- And he was really
confident and you know,

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.430
and he has these like runner's lungs,

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:08.290
and he was underwater
for a solid two minutes,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.200
trying to impress my family.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.962
- [Kelly] He's gonna die
trying to impress your dad.

00:03:11.962 --> 00:03:12.795
- Yeah.

00:03:12.795 --> 00:03:13.628
- [Justin] Ice cold water?

00:03:13.628 --> 00:03:14.461
- Ice cold water, yeah.

00:03:14.461 --> 00:03:15.294
- That's great, that's commitment,

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:16.127
You knew right then didn't you?

00:03:16.127 --> 00:03:17.938
- I did, he was the one, he beat my dad.

00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:19.280
- [Kelly] He's committed
and he wants to win.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.067
I like it, I would be
attracted to that too.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:21.900
(laughs loudly)

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.220
But tell us about your
new show though, Indebted.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.810
- Indebted, it is about baby boomers,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.780
played by Fran Drescher and Steven Weber,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.650
who lose all their money and go broke,

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.650
and they have to move in

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.250
with their young son and his family,

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.440
and I play the wife of the son.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.590
- [Kelly] Whose super excited.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.840
- Whose super excited

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.570
to have her in-laws move in.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.980
And yeah, it's a lot.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.770
So my character is kinda caught

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:49.110
in the middle of this
crazy new family dynamic

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.700
that's happening in her house,

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.970
and it's a really fun,

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.340
we have such a great time.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.490
- [Kelly] I love personally,

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.160
both of your shows I think represent

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.750
like actual real
conversations that happen,

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.190
be it funny or serious,

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.630
and I think that's so important,

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:03.590
it's fun to watch

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.170
and know that you're not abnormal,

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.470
that so many families go through

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.950
all of those experiences and emotions.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.150
- [Abby] Totally, and the
show really dives into,

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.620
you know, what it's like to be a boomer

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.619
who doesn't know how to use technology

00:04:16.619 --> 00:04:18.670
and then we're the millennials

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.040
who are like, "Uh.",

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.880
but we're also learning from them,

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.990
